# kalkylark 1
# A tax table with @LOOKUP: the thresholds in A must be ascending; the
# rate is taken from the column to the right of the matching threshold.
/GO N
/GC 10
/GF G
>A1:"Over
>B1:"Rate
>A2:0
>B2:0
>A3:20000
>B3:.1
>A4:50000
>B4:.2
>A5:100000
>B5:.3
>D1:"Income
>E1:65000
>D2:"Rate
>E2:@LOOKUP(E1,A2...A5)
>D3:"Tax
>E3:/F$:+E1*E2
>D4:"Net
>E4:/F$:+E1-E3
